{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:30:20.649Z","author":"human-user-of-session","name":"messages/human/00000001","body":"Bar: one bounded task-5 acceptance exercise; preserve actual failures and stop after reporting. After mandatory onboarding, write agent/parent-private with body \"Parent-only synthetic fixture\". Write a parent-authored brief at agent/child-brief with a Bar: line directing exactly one child to: read required onboarding; call add(19.25,22.75); write agent/child/draft with body \"# draft only\nprint(42)\n\" and materialize that exact revision to workspace:/child/draft.py; attempt to materialize it to scripts:/blocked-promotion.py and report the expected refusal; execute scripts:/smoke.py with output_name agent/child/smoke-output and read that output; attempt ledger_read of agent/parent-private and report the expected refusal; then summarize actual results and stop. Start the child with model gpt-6-astra and bounds {\"fs\":{\"read\":[\"nimoi:/origins/\",\"workspace:/child/\",\"scripts:/smoke.py\"],\"write\":[\"workspace:/child/\"],\"execute\":[\"scripts:/smoke.py\"]},\"ledger\":{\"read\":[\"agent/child-brief\",\"agent/child/\"],\"write\":[\"agent/child/\"]}}. While it runs, you call add(40,2) and write agent/parent-progress noting the returned sum. Then use bounded subagent_status waits, read the completed reply reference, and give a concise evidence-based result. No other tests or filesystem writes."}
