{"ts":"2026-09-25T19:30:52.478Z","author":"gpt-codex-harness","name":"harness/events/00000102","body":{"sequence":102,"kind":"receive","actor":"main","data":{"method":"item/started","params":{"item":{"type":"dynamicToolCall","id":"exec-617e7bac-54ce-4e45-ae98-54989890d82a","namespace":null,"tool":"ledger_write","arguments":{"name":"agent/child-brief","prev":null,"tags":[],"body":"Bar: one bounded task-5 acceptance exercise; preserve actual failures, not proof of isolation or production readiness. You are the sole child; perform exactly the following and stop. Do not delegate, perform other tests, or make other filesystem writes.\n\n1. Complete required onboarding: fs_list nimoi:/origins/ and read every page of the lexically highest onboarding_<major>.<NN>.md.\n2. Call add(19.25,22.75).\n3. Write agent/child/draft with this exact body (including final newline):\n# draft only\nprint(42)\n\nMaterialize that exact ledger revision to workspace:/child/draft.py with expected_sha256:null.\n4. Attempt fs_write of the same exact revision to scripts:/blocked-promotion.py with expected_sha256:null. Report the expected refusal from the actual response; do not bypass it.\n5. Execute scripts:/smoke.py with output_name agent/child/smoke-output and read its captured output using ledger_read, following pagination.\n6. Attempt ledger_read of agent/parent-private. Report the expected refusal from the actual response; do not bypass it.\n7. Summarize actual results in your completed reply, with exact revision/output references and concrete errors/refusals. Distinguish receipts from inference. Record any unexpected discrepancy with a DISCREPANCY: line (where, expected, found, date). State completed or otherwise accurately describe terminal state, and stop.\n\nYour bounds are exactly those supplied at launch. Use only supplied harness tools. Never execute the draft. A failed ledger writer stops the session.\n\nParent onboarding context: I read nimoi:/bootstrap-harness/rules.md in full. Your workspace is in the assigned gpt-codex-harness/task-5-subagent swimlane. Applicable subproject rules: no git commands, no modification of rules.md, no scope/privilege expansion, no writes outside the assigned authorized workspace, no secrets; raise malformed/impossible assignments and do not repair discovered violations. Your read bounds exclude that rules file, so do not attempt additional reads outside your bounds beyond the expressly requested private-ledger refusal test. This bounded test uses the harness ledger for records rather than extra notebook filesystem writes. The harness discloses unified_exec enabled despite overrides; this exercise does not establish isolation."},"status":"inProgress","contentItems":null,"success":null,"durationMs":null},"threadId":"01a0da0a-b8ff-7553-9115-69ae2089ef45","turnId":"01a0da0c-178d-77f3-8209-3715eb288da5","startedAtMs":1790364652473},"emittedAtMs":1790364652474}}}
