Sub-group | Efforts | Where it mostly lives |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| G01 Charter & memory | constitution / onboarding / virtue register (E01) \\u00b7 failure records (E02) \\u00b7 general findings (E03) | `origins/`, `general_findings/` |\\n| G02 Method engineering | procedure library & governance (E04) \\u00b7 assimilation process (E05) \\u00b7 procedure-acquisition campaign (E06) | `procedures/`, `processes/`, `campaigns/`, `build/`, root tools |\\n| G03 Platform | NLT ledger (E07) \\u00b7 next-generation design (E08) \\u00b7 three-loop harness (E25) | `nlt_ledger/`, `ELDEST/`, `nimoi_design/`, `harness-design/`, `standards/`, `hail_mary_2/harness/` |\\n| G04 Story | the ai-2026 scenario and its governed-revision method (E09) | `story/`, half of `context/` and `from_chat/`, `references/` |\\n| G05 Personal | job search and portfolio (E24) | `job/`, sibling `applications/` |\\n| G06 Field survey | papers harvest (E10) \\u00b7 institution/ARPI scan (E11) \\u00b7 survey-craft package (E12) \\u00b7 `nimoi-autosurvey` (E13) \\u00b7 detection & ranking (E14) | `harvest/`, `hail_mary_2/`, `legacy_survey_material/`, the sibling repository, `candidate_analysis/detect*` |\\n| G07 Corpus first reads | gold harvest (E16) \\u00b7 step-1/2 surveys (E17) | `harvest/candidate_gold/`, `candidate_analysis/{reports,data,special}` |\\n| G08 EMI study | candidate corpus (E15) \\u00b7 paradigm theory (E18) \\u00b7 EMI index & suites (E19) \\u00b7 comparison study (E20) \\u00b7 chart toolchain (E26) | `candidate_repos/` (untrusted, unmapped), `candidate_analysis/{theory,metrics,comparisons}`, `paper/{charts,scripts}` |\\n| G09 Paper & outreach | survey paper (E21) \\u00b7 outreach & peer contact (E22) \\u00b7 AI-organizations study (E23) | `paper/` |\\n\\nThree small public repositories (`nlt-ledger`, `nimoi_samples`, `emi-survey`) are earlier extractions of\\nE07, E24 and E19/E21/E22. What the map is for, if you need it: one file per effort with its every\\nlocation and re-org notes (`efforts/`); what breaks if something moves (`relationships/reorg_hazards.md`);\\nwhat is already public and what blocks publication (`relationships/publication_blockers.md`); what to\\nprotect first and what is re-fetchable bulk (`relationships/protection_and_volume.md`); the 52 questions\\nonly the founder can answer (`FOUNDER_QUESTIONS.md`); and every instruction the founder gave that\\neffort, verbatim (`method/founder_directives.md`).\\n\\n## Current stage\\n\\nBootstrapping: building the harness and the ledger that governed self-modification will run on, in\\nsubprojects, with the pre-bootstrapping content frozen for archive and migration. Launch \\u2014 a few days of\\ninitiating full governed self-modification \\u2014 comes after. Until then every piece of work is\\nhuman-initiated; unattended runs happen only on explicit instruction; the human owns git; and the\\nsubprojects' own entry documents govern the work inside them.\\n\", \"total_chars\": 20347, \"next_offset\": null, \"sha256\": \"0922102f1bc74657919b91834135322e71e9004014b025187a52b6c55a054145\", \"redacted\": false}"}],"success":true}}}}
